  "gamePlayAgain": "Play again",
  "lesson1Card1Title": "What is a variable?",
  "@lesson1Card1Speech": {
    "description": "Lesson text. Very simple English: 8-10 words per sentence, one idea each. Words in `backticks` are code: keep them in English."
  },
  "lesson1Card1Speech": "Beep boop! I am Cog. Robots need to remember things. I remember my battery in a variable. A variable is like a box. The box has a name on it. The thing inside is the value.",
  "lesson1Card1Tip": "A variable is a box with a name. It holds a value.",
  "lesson1Card2Title": "Notes in code",
  "lesson1Card2Speech": "You can write notes in your code. A note starts with `#`. We call it a comment. A comment is a note for people. Python skips it completely. It does nothing to the code. It only helps people read the code.",
  "lesson1Card2Tip": "Python skips everything after `#` on that line.",
  "lesson1Card3Title": "Making a variable",
  "lesson1Card3Speech": "Let's make a variable! First, write the name. Next, write `=`. Last, write the value. The `=` means \"put this in the box.\"",
  "lesson1Card3Tip": "In Python, `=` does not mean \"equal.\" It means \"put this value in the box.\"",
  "lesson1Card4Title": "Kinds of values",
  "lesson1Card4Speech": "A box can hold different kinds of values. It can hold a number, like `5`. It can hold a word in quotes, like `\"Cog\"`. It can hold `True` or `False`. They mean yes or no.",
  "lesson1Card4Tip": "Words need quotes. Numbers do not. `True` and `False` start with a big letter.",
  "lesson1Card5Title": "Changing a variable",
  "lesson1Card5Speech": "I walked a lot. My battery went down! Let's change it. Python reads code from top to bottom. First, the box gets 100. Then, the box gets 80. The 100 is gone. Now the box has 80.",
  "lesson1Card5Tip": "A box keeps only its newest value.",
  "lesson1Card6Title": "Naming rules",
  "lesson1Card6Speech": "Every box needs a good name. Follow my rules:\n• No spaces. Use `_` instead.\n• Do not start with a number.\n• Big and small letters are different. `speed` and `Speed` are two boxes!\n• Pick a name that makes sense.",
  "lesson1Card6Tip": "Good names help people read your code.",
  "@lesson1NoteBattery100": {
    "description": "Arrow note shown after a code line (\"← note\"). Plain, short words. Variable names like battery stay in English."
  },
  "lesson1NoteBattery100": "battery is now 100",
  "lesson1NoteSpeed5": "speed is now the number 5",
  "lesson1NoteRobotName": "robot_name is now the word Cog",
  "lesson1NoteIsMoving": "is_moving is now True (yes)",
  "lesson1NoteBattery80": "battery is now 80. The 100 is gone.",
  "lesson1NoteGoodUnderscore": "Good! _ takes the place of the space",
  "lesson1NoteBadSpace": "No spaces allowed",
  "lesson1NoteGoodNumberEnd": "OK! The number is at the end",
  "lesson1NoteBadNumberStart": "Can't start with a number",
  "lesson1NoteSpeedSmall": "speed is one box",
  "lesson1NoteSpeedBig": "Speed is a different box!",
  "lesson1NoteGoodClear": "Clear name",
  "lesson1NoteBadUnclear": "What is b? Not clear.",
  "@quiz1Q1Prompt": {
    "description": "Quiz text. Hints (…Why…) must be gentle, 1-2 short sentences, and must not reveal the right answer. Words in `backticks` are code: keep them in English."
  },
  "quiz1Q1Prompt": "What is a variable?",
  "quiz1Q1Right": "A box with a name that holds a value",
  "quiz1Q1WrongRobot": "A kind of robot",
  "quiz1Q1WhyRobot": "Not quite! A variable is not a robot. A robot uses it to remember.",
  "quiz1Q1WrongCommand": "A command that turns on the robot",
  "quiz1Q1WhyCommand": "Good guess! But a variable does not do things. It holds a value.",
  "quiz1Q1Explain": "A variable is a box with a name. The value goes inside.",
  "quiz1Q2Prompt": "In this code, what does `=` do?",
  "quiz1Q2Right": "It puts `5` in the box `speed`",
  "quiz1Q2WrongCheck": "It checks if `speed` equals `5`",
  "quiz1Q2WhyCheck": "That is how `=` works in math. Python uses it in a different way.",
  "quiz1Q2WrongDelete": "It deletes `speed`",
  "quiz1Q2WhyDelete": "Nothing gets deleted here. Think about the box!",
  "quiz1Q2Explain": "In Python, `=` means \"put this in the box.\" So `5` goes in `speed`.",
  "quiz1Q3Prompt": "What kind of value is this?",
  "quiz1Q3Right": "A word (text)",
  "quiz1Q3WrongNumber": "A number",
  "quiz1Q3WhyNumber": "Look at the quotes! Numbers do not use quotes.",
  "quiz1Q3WrongBool": "True or False",
  "quiz1Q3WhyBool": "`True` and `False` have no quotes. This value has quotes.",
  "quiz1Q3Explain": "Words in quotes are text. So `\"Cog\"` is text.",
  "quiz1Q4Prompt": "After this code runs, what is in `battery`?",
  "quiz1Q4Why100": "That was the first value. What came next?",
  "quiz1Q4Why180": "Values do not add up. Think about the old value.",
  "quiz1Q4Explain": "First the box had 100. Then 80 took its place. Now `battery` is `80`.",
  "quiz1Q5Prompt": "Which one is a good variable name?",
  "quiz1Q5WhyNumberStart": "Look at the first letter. Remember the number rule?",
  "quiz1Q5WhySpace": "Look at the space in the middle. Remember the space rule?",
  "quiz1Q5Explain": "`robot_name` has no spaces. It does not start with a number. It makes sense.",
  "@game1R1Intro": {
    "description": "Game text. Intros give the story clues; hints are ONE gentle sentence and must not shame. Text in quotes like \"Cog\" or `code` is code: keep it in English."
  },
  "game1R1Intro": "Help me fill my boxes! Each value has one box.",
  "game1R1HintCog": "\"Cog\" has quotes, so it is a word. Which box is for a name?",
  "game1R1HintTeal": "\"teal\" is a color, not a name.",
  "game1R1Hint80": "80 is a big number. Which box can be 80% full?",
  "game1R1Hint4": "4 is a small number. How many wheels can a robot have?",
  "game1R2Intro": "This is my friend Bolt! Bolt moves at speed 5. Bolt lives in Manila.",
  "game1R2HintBolt": "\"Bolt\" is my friend's name.",
  "game1R2Hint5": "5 is a number. Which box tells how fast?",
  "game1R2HintTrue": "True means yes. Find the box that asks a yes-or-no question!",
  "game1R2HintManila": "Manila is a place, not a robot name.",
  "game1R3Intro": "Oops! I walked 250 steps. My battery went down to 60. I am not charging yet. Fix my boxes!",
  "game1R3Hint60": "60 is my new battery. Put it in the box that needs a change.",
  "game1R3HintCog": "\"Cog\" is my name. Find the name box!",
  "game1R3HintFalse": "False means no. Find the box that asks yes or no.",
  "game1R3Hint250": "250 is how many steps I walked.",
